WEBVTT

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:06.600
For LFG to finance your company 
again, I have two conditions.

00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:10.270
First, show me what you are capable of.

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:12.760
If, after the airing of the next episode,

00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:16.560
<i>Miracle Finder</i> is trending on 
social media in the top ten,

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:19.830
I will acknowledge that you have the 
minimum production capability required.

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:22.200
Th-That'll be easy.

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:24.410
I'm confident in the content  
for our next program.

00:00:24.410 --> 00:00:27.030
Second, you will assemble 
a comprehensive business plan

00:00:27.030 --> 00:00:29.800
and submit it to me within a week.

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:33.300
In five years, I will stand 
at the top of this industry!

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:35.460
Per your declaration,

00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:39.130
draw a blueprint of how you will reach 
the top of your industry in five years,

00:00:39.130 --> 00:00:40.640
and convince me it will work.

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:43.380
Yes, sir.

00:00:43.380 --> 00:00:44.250
That is all.

00:00:44.590 --> 00:00:48.410
If you meet the conditions, 
I will re-evaluate your financing.

00:00:48.410 --> 00:00:49.380
Evaluate?

00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:51.310
Not "reinstate" our financing?

00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:55.020
Thank you.

00:00:55.020 --> 00:00:57.540
I will not waste the chance you have given us.

00:00:57.540 --> 00:01:00.610
It would have been easier to just give up, yes?

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:05.080
No.

00:01:05.390 --> 00:01:07.610
It's true I was acting on impulse earlier.

00:01:08.620 --> 00:01:09.980
But you're right.

00:01:09.980 --> 00:01:12.110
In order for us to survive,

00:01:12.110 --> 00:01:15.760
a strong desire and determination 
to reach the top is crucial.

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:18.710
To make my dream come true,

00:01:18.710 --> 00:01:21.600
I will show you I can meet your demands.

00:01:23.180 --> 00:01:25.150
Those who rest on their laurels,

00:01:25.150 --> 00:01:28.130
and those who hide within the status quo, 
do not pique my interest.

00:01:28.130 --> 00:01:32.570
I invest in the determination and power
 to break open a new future.

00:01:33.240 --> 00:01:36.580
Show me. Prove your potential.

00:01:36.920 --> 00:01:37.700
I will.

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:39.090
If you'll excuse me.

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:42.370
Did you discuss what happened
 this afternoon with anyone?

00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:49.490
<i>I only asked Professor Lucien 
about Evolvers, so...</i>

00:01:49.490 --> 00:01:51.380
<i>I didn't say anything, right? I said nothing.</i>

00:01:51.380 --> 00:01:52.720
<i>Okay. I'm good!</i>

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:54.340
I've said nothing.

00:01:55.490 --> 00:01:56.620
Good.

00:02:01.970 --> 00:02:03.360
I thought...

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:06.620
it was a secret... Right?

00:02:06.950 --> 00:02:09.150
I'm not taking any particular pains to hide it.

00:02:09.660 --> 00:02:10.520
That said,

00:02:10.520 --> 00:02:13.940
I'd rather not be subjected to senseless 
investigations by inane fools.

00:02:14.270 --> 00:02:17.080
I see... Is that all?

00:02:17.080 --> 00:02:20.120
If it were me, I think 
I might be a little bit happy.

00:02:20.120 --> 00:02:22.800
Having a special power that other 
people don't would be super—

00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:24.980
You seem quite calm.

00:02:25.450 --> 00:02:29.080
Shall I move the deadline for your 
business plan up to tomorrow morning?

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:31.540
Sorry to have bothered you!

00:02:37.210 --> 00:02:41.090
<i>At the time, I thought the 
existence of special powers</i>

00:02:41.090 --> 00:02:43.510
<i>was something from another 
world, for other people.</i>

00:02:44.250 --> 00:02:46.920
<i>Everything had already started long ago...</i>

00:02:47.340 --> 00:02:49.050
<i>though I hadn't noticed it.</i>

00:02:51.310 --> 00:03:00.320
"It takes all the running you can do, 
to keep in the same place."

00:02:51.310 --> 00:03:00.320
~The Red Queen Hypothesis~

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:06.590
<i>In this world, there exist 
unique powers known as "Evol,"</i>

00:03:06.590 --> 00:03:08.830
<i>which are possessed by a very few.</i>

00:03:09.320 --> 00:03:13.250
<i>Among them, some chose to fight 
their fate, to fight the world.</i>

00:03:13.250 --> 00:03:15.900
<i>This is the story of these young "Evolvers."</i>

00:04:31.410 --> 00:04:36.000
<b>Mr. Love: Queen's Choice</b>

00:04:36.330 --> 00:04:38.960
"When the Wind Blows"

00:05:03.640 --> 00:05:06.050
What... was that?

00:05:06.050 --> 00:05:08.240
Huh? A dream?

00:05:09.490 --> 00:05:11.700
I still haven't gotten anything together!

00:05:09.490 --> 00:05:11.700
Miracle Entertainment
 Business Plan

00:05:11.700 --> 00:05:13.540
And I'm late on top of that!

00:05:14.730 --> 00:05:16.080
I can't take this!

00:05:22.070 --> 00:05:24.300
I-I'm sorry! Excuse me!

00:05:27.420 --> 00:05:32.190
Which is how the phenomenon of 
suddenly warping to another location

00:05:32.190 --> 00:05:36.430
can be explained through the application 
of this theory of folding space.

00:05:37.490 --> 00:05:38.730
Any questions?

00:05:38.730 --> 00:05:40.720
Hold on, President!

00:05:40.720 --> 00:05:43.680
Where did you find this hot professor?

00:05:43.680 --> 00:05:44.910
It's perfect.

00:05:44.910 --> 00:05:46.690
If he appears on our show,

00:05:46.690 --> 00:05:51.060
our production quality, ratings, and 
viewership will skyrocket. No question.

00:05:51.060 --> 00:05:53.200
C-Calm down, both of you.

00:05:53.200 --> 00:05:55.690
Actually, that hurts! Ow, ow, ow!

00:05:55.690 --> 00:05:58.960
The conditions from LFG 
seem quite difficult to meet.

00:05:59.560 --> 00:06:01.500
As I've agreed to be a consultant,

00:06:01.500 --> 00:06:03.870
I'll help in any way I can.

00:06:04.330 --> 00:06:07.010
Thank you, Professor Lucien.

00:06:07.010 --> 00:06:08.750
We look forward to working with you.

00:06:09.470 --> 00:06:12.640
Now, for my first suggestion...

00:06:12.640 --> 00:06:16.320
Shall we agree to stop speaking 
so formally with each other?

00:06:16.740 --> 00:06:19.930
We are all working to make 
this show together, after all.

00:06:22.260 --> 00:06:23.530
I see.

00:06:23.530 --> 00:06:27.130
The boy you met yesterday is an Evolver,

00:06:27.130 --> 00:06:31.450
and you believe he's at the center 
of the string of incidents.

00:06:31.770 --> 00:06:32.620
Yes.

00:06:33.080 --> 00:06:35.370
But is all that really true?

00:06:35.370 --> 00:06:38.190
President, are you sure you weren't 
just so tired, you started dreaming?

00:06:38.190 --> 00:06:42.240
Most of our viewers will have
the same reaction as you.

00:06:42.240 --> 00:06:45.820
That's why I've been saying we should make 
a show that will convince them. Right?

00:06:45.820 --> 00:06:50.600
Well, if we could get testimony from 
that boy, that would cinch things, but...

00:06:50.600 --> 00:06:53.100
He warped and disappeared, right?

00:06:53.100 --> 00:06:57.030
There's no way even a pro police 
officer could find someone like that.

00:06:58.250 --> 00:06:59.940
Police, huh?

00:06:59.940 --> 00:07:03.400
That boy... It seemed like he was being chased.

00:07:03.690 --> 00:07:05.810
He might have gone to the police for help...

00:07:05.810 --> 00:07:08.130
Or if he has family, they might 
have asked for a search.

00:07:08.130 --> 00:07:09.520
There should be records.

00:07:09.520 --> 00:07:11.790
You mean we should try to 
get info from the police?

00:07:11.790 --> 00:07:12.550
Yes.

00:07:12.550 --> 00:07:15.350
We don't really have any connections 
in the press department, though.

00:07:15.350 --> 00:07:19.260
There were a few who knew 
your father when he was here,

00:07:19.710 --> 00:07:21.310
but I don't know about now.

00:07:21.310 --> 00:07:23.000
Among the victims of the warp incidents,

00:07:23.000 --> 00:07:25.740
there was one who was thrown into
 the mountains and couldn't get home,

00:07:25.740 --> 00:07:29.290
so the family asked for 
a search to be conducted.

00:07:29.290 --> 00:07:31.680
You may be able to find
information along those lines.

00:07:38.470 --> 00:07:40.480
<i>I rushed over here all fired up,</i>

00:07:40.770 --> 00:07:42.850
<i>but it might not work out so well after all...</i>

00:07:42.850 --> 00:07:45.860
<i>I mean, the person who was 
helping me hasn't come back yet.</i>

00:07:47.290 --> 00:07:48.880
Uh, Miracle...

00:07:48.880 --> 00:07:50.530
Miracle something-or-other?

00:07:50.530 --> 00:07:51.810
Someone from TV?

00:07:51.810 --> 00:07:52.850
Oh, yes!

00:07:53.540 --> 00:07:54.670
Who are you?

00:07:54.670 --> 00:07:55.670
I'm sorry?

00:07:55.670 --> 00:07:59.400
Sticking your nose into a case run 
by Detective Gavin, of all people,

00:07:59.400 --> 00:08:02.140
and he gives you clearance to 
investigate just like that...

00:08:02.140 --> 00:08:04.040
Ah, here's your pass.

00:08:04.640 --> 00:08:05.730
Thank you.

00:08:05.730 --> 00:08:07.210
You got connections at the top or what?

00:08:07.210 --> 00:08:08.770
Huh? No...

00:08:08.770 --> 00:08:12.510
Detective Gavin is supposed to be some
 higher-up's son or something, but...

00:08:12.510 --> 00:08:13.880
<i>Huh? Gavin?</i>

00:08:13.880 --> 00:08:15.720
He just floats around all day, every day.

00:08:15.720 --> 00:08:18.000
I can't tell if he's investigating or goofing off.

00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:20.040
And the section chief never says a thing to him.

00:08:20.040 --> 00:08:22.170
I hope you make it home alive...

00:08:22.810 --> 00:08:23.520
Hey.

00:08:23.520 --> 00:08:25.000
Y-Yes!

00:08:25.320 --> 00:08:27.740
Are you the detective in charge?

00:08:28.350 --> 00:08:29.580
Thank you for your help today—

00:08:29.580 --> 00:08:31.450
You're being way too formal.

00:08:31.450 --> 00:08:32.240
Huh?

00:08:34.250 --> 00:08:35.570
It's been a while.

00:08:42.650 --> 00:08:43.750
What?!

00:08:43.750 --> 00:08:45.520
Wait, are you Gavin-senpai?

00:08:45.520 --> 00:08:47.320
Huh? Wait, how?

00:08:47.320 --> 00:08:48.880
Gavin-senpai is a detective?!

00:08:48.880 --> 00:08:50.380
Did you forget?

00:08:50.380 --> 00:08:51.550
Or is it...

00:08:51.860 --> 00:08:55.590
You thought I'd end up in police custody
 rather than on the force?

00:08:56.490 --> 00:08:57.680
You little...

00:08:57.680 --> 00:09:01.810
<i>Gavin-senpai was my senpai in high 
school, two years ahead of me.</i>

00:09:02.560 --> 00:09:04.390
<i>At the time, he had a really bad reputation,</i>

00:09:04.390 --> 00:09:06.450
<i>and everyone was afraid of him.</i>

00:09:07.100 --> 00:09:10.540
<i>I ended up seeing what appeared 
to be him blackmailing someone.</i>

00:09:10.540 --> 00:09:11.730
<i>After that...</i>

00:09:12.760 --> 00:09:14.990
<i>He sent me a note calling me out.</i>

00:09:14.990 --> 00:09:18.740
Gavin

00:09:14.990 --> 00:09:18.740
<i>I was so terrified, 
I ended up standing him up.</i>

00:09:19.850 --> 00:09:22.290
<i>I wonder if he still remembers that.</i>

00:09:22.290 --> 00:09:24.830
Wait, huh? Gavin-senpai?

00:09:24.830 --> 00:09:27.600
Wait, Senpai! Where are you going?

00:09:27.600 --> 00:09:28.560
Crime scene.

00:09:33.680 --> 00:09:34.920
Um...

00:09:35.340 --> 00:09:36.470
I'm sorry.

00:09:36.470 --> 00:09:39.310
Right now, I'm working as 
a producer on a TV show.

00:09:39.310 --> 00:09:41.580
I came to investigate... I mean...

00:09:41.580 --> 00:09:44.400
I wanted to ask about the warping incidents.

00:09:44.400 --> 00:09:48.350
How can I put this... I only just found out 
that you're overseeing the cases...

00:09:48.350 --> 00:09:50.150
Put this on.

00:09:50.150 --> 00:09:50.950
Here.

00:09:51.670 --> 00:09:53.680
It's faster if you see it for yourself.

00:09:54.470 --> 00:09:56.530
If you want to know more, come with me.

00:10:01.000 --> 00:10:02.700
I-If you don't mind.

00:10:10.510 --> 00:10:11.660
You'll die like that.

00:10:11.660 --> 00:10:12.710
What?

00:10:31.360 --> 00:10:32.720
I almost died...

00:10:32.720 --> 00:10:34.690
I really thought I was gonna die...

00:10:34.690 --> 00:10:36.150
You gonna rest there?

00:10:36.620 --> 00:10:38.280
No! I'm coming, too!

00:10:43.230 --> 00:10:44.800
I'm telling you in advance.

00:10:44.800 --> 00:10:47.700
What lies ahead is far more 
dangerous than you imagine.

00:10:48.130 --> 00:10:50.440
Yesterday's events ended without incident,

00:10:50.440 --> 00:10:52.200
only because they believed

00:10:52.200 --> 00:10:54.290
that you were just an innocent bystander.

00:10:57.300 --> 00:11:01.120
Gavin-senpai, you were there yesterday?

00:11:06.530 --> 00:11:10.350
But I can't give up here, 
either. No matter what.

00:11:31.620 --> 00:11:35.000
<b>Mr. Love: Queen's Choice</b>

00:11:36.630 --> 00:11:40.010
<b>Mr. Love: Queen's Choice</b>

00:11:45.850 --> 00:11:49.430
The target disappeared from his home 
approximately three months ago.

00:11:49.970 --> 00:11:52.140
It seemed at first to be 
a simple runaway case,

00:11:52.140 --> 00:11:54.420
but last week, he suddenly returned.

00:11:56.220 --> 00:11:58.990
It seems he'd been moving from
 part-time job to part-time job.

00:12:03.330 --> 00:12:04.800
Why...

00:12:04.800 --> 00:12:07.880
The incidents started happening 
about six months ago.

00:12:08.440 --> 00:12:11.310
Initially, they occurred in the evenings.

00:12:11.310 --> 00:12:13.580
They were limited to the time 
after schools let out.

00:12:14.170 --> 00:12:16.160
The distances of the warps were very short.

00:12:16.160 --> 00:12:18.920
At most, they were moved to the next block.

00:12:19.310 --> 00:12:22.200
It was probably someone testing 
a newly awakened power,

00:12:22.200 --> 00:12:23.680
playing some simple pranks.

00:12:30.720 --> 00:12:32.430
But that power attracted attention

00:12:32.430 --> 00:12:34.310
from certain people, who then showed up.

00:12:36.100 --> 00:12:38.960
There was a sudden shift 
in the pattern of the warping.

00:12:39.560 --> 00:12:41.400
Changes in both direction and time.

00:12:41.690 --> 00:12:44.080
A fixed distance was repeated over and over,

00:12:44.080 --> 00:12:45.640
day after day,

00:12:45.950 --> 00:12:49.030
like some kind of training 
exercise... or an experiment.

00:12:51.380 --> 00:12:54.510
The pattern changed three months ago,

00:12:55.130 --> 00:12:57.630
just about the time the boy disappeared.

00:12:58.320 --> 00:12:59.780
That means...

00:13:01.110 --> 00:13:04.010
He didn't run away from home. 
He was kidnapped.

00:13:07.070 --> 00:13:09.670
When he appeared one week ago in this city,

00:13:09.980 --> 00:13:11.980
it's likely because he escaped.

00:13:12.920 --> 00:13:17.230
The reason he didn't return home was 
to avoid getting his family involved.

00:13:18.140 --> 00:13:22.860
It's possible that boy... 
was hoping for help from me.

00:13:24.280 --> 00:13:27.630
Please! Won't you listen to my story?

00:13:27.630 --> 00:13:29.630
If you're from TV, I just know—

00:13:33.750 --> 00:13:35.710
No need to worry.

00:13:36.040 --> 00:13:38.580
We'll take that boy into protection.

00:13:42.960 --> 00:13:45.260
Keeping people with special powers from

00:13:45.260 --> 00:13:48.070
getting involved in any crimes 
caused by those powers...

00:13:48.070 --> 00:13:49.630
That's what we do

00:13:49.630 --> 00:13:51.930
in the Evolver Anti-Crime Special Task Force.

00:13:52.690 --> 00:13:54.060
Evolvers...

00:13:54.060 --> 00:13:55.270
You know about them?

00:13:55.270 --> 00:13:56.090
Huh?

00:13:56.090 --> 00:13:58.630
In my investigations, um...

00:14:00.760 --> 00:14:03.690
He's been pushing his warp ability 
to run from place to place,

00:14:03.690 --> 00:14:05.440
but he should be reaching his limits soon.

00:14:06.240 --> 00:14:07.630
Before that, we should—

00:14:15.560 --> 00:14:17.120
Gavin-senpai?

00:14:17.120 --> 00:14:17.990
Wait...

00:14:17.990 --> 00:14:20.760
This is the place I saw in my dream...

00:14:21.420 --> 00:14:24.820
By just strolling along like that, 
you've saved us a lot of trouble.

00:14:24.820 --> 00:14:28.870
To think you were acquainted with an 
investigator from the Special Task Force.

00:14:29.550 --> 00:14:30.340
Who is that?

00:14:30.340 --> 00:14:31.930
And, wait... a knife?

00:14:32.230 --> 00:14:34.600
<i>It can't be... Are they trying to silence me?</i>

00:14:36.080 --> 00:14:38.090
It's just orders, you see.

00:14:47.350 --> 00:14:48.280
You little...

00:14:48.900 --> 00:14:51.010
Keep still, damn it!

00:14:54.080 --> 00:14:54.870
Stay down!

00:14:59.820 --> 00:15:01.210
Get up! Run! Jump!

00:15:01.210 --> 00:15:01.960
G-Got it!

00:15:17.640 --> 00:15:19.410
Don't hesitate! Jump!

00:15:29.770 --> 00:15:31.060
Good work. You did it.

00:15:32.730 --> 00:15:34.170
Gavin-senpai?

00:15:35.940 --> 00:15:36.990
How...

00:15:39.260 --> 00:15:42.960
As long as you are somewhere 
in the wind, I will always find you.

00:15:48.490 --> 00:15:51.480
<i>Gavin-senpai... is an Evolver, too.</i>

00:15:59.290 --> 00:16:01.460
That must have been scary for you.

00:16:01.460 --> 00:16:03.210
Wait just a little longer for me.

00:16:05.290 --> 00:16:06.110
Huh?

00:16:06.110 --> 00:16:07.170
This is the roof!

00:16:07.480 --> 00:16:08.780
Huh? Senpai!

00:16:08.780 --> 00:16:11.570
Damn it... For now, I need to report—

00:16:11.570 --> 00:16:12.860
Come, now.

00:16:12.860 --> 00:16:14.320
Did you think I'd let you get away?

00:16:20.560 --> 00:16:22.160
Damn it.

00:16:23.670 --> 00:16:25.130
There's no need to be afraid!

00:16:25.790 --> 00:16:28.280
Our unit will take you under its protection!

00:16:38.140 --> 00:16:40.780
They used his family to threaten him,

00:16:40.780 --> 00:16:43.440
making him warp you to that alley.

00:16:43.900 --> 00:16:45.450
After he's interviewed,

00:16:45.450 --> 00:16:48.190
for the time being, 
we'll take him into protection.

00:16:53.200 --> 00:16:55.430
He can't go back to his family?

00:16:55.820 --> 00:16:58.340
Not until we can secure everyone's safety.

00:16:58.340 --> 00:17:03.220
Their organization targets people 
with special powers, Evolvers.

00:17:03.220 --> 00:17:05.710
And what is this organization?

00:17:07.100 --> 00:17:08.290
Black Swan.

00:17:15.070 --> 00:17:16.410
What will you do?

00:17:16.410 --> 00:17:17.200
Huh?

00:17:17.540 --> 00:17:20.310
Are you going to use this case in your show?

00:17:21.180 --> 00:17:25.170
Even we don't know the full story 
behind Black Swan yet.

00:17:25.480 --> 00:17:28.970
If the existence of Evolvers 
is treated too lightly,

00:17:28.970 --> 00:17:31.440
there's no telling how the 
general public will react.

00:17:31.440 --> 00:17:35.570
I'd rather not be subjected to senseless 
investigations by inane fools.

00:17:37.640 --> 00:17:41.240
I understand that it isn't something 
to stir up just to satisfy my curiosity.

00:17:41.240 --> 00:17:45.890
But if there's someone who wants to
 use Evolver powers for their own ends,

00:17:45.890 --> 00:17:48.550
then I don't think I can 
just leave things alone.

00:17:49.300 --> 00:17:51.010
I'll think about how to handle it.

00:17:51.010 --> 00:17:53.110
I don't know anything about anything yet...

00:17:53.110 --> 00:17:54.680
I know it won't be easy.

00:17:55.160 --> 00:17:57.480
But I want to know the truth.

00:17:57.480 --> 00:18:00.330
